  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Changes were made. This is not a verbatim republication of the original
Microsoft Learn pages. The content in this repository has been:

  - restructured and, in most pages, substantially expanded with
    additional conceptual framing, worked examples, and cross-links not
    present in the original source, while every API name, type, method,
    config key, default value, and version claim remains grounded in the
    original source text;
  - re-authored as Markdown with a custom compiler (see
    yarp-docs/content/README.md) rather than copied HTML;
  - translated into Bulgarian, Russian, French, Greek, Spanish, German,
    Portuguese (Brazil), and Simplified Chinese, in addition to the
    original English.

Each individual page in yarp-docs/content/ records its own specific
Microsoft Learn source URL in its `sourceUrl` frontmatter field, and every
compiled page displays a per-page attribution line linking back to that
exact source and to the CC BY 4.0 license, in the reader's own language
(see the `article.attribution` translation key in each of
yarp-docs/public/assets/i18n/*.json).

Source PDFs
-----------

The 36 PDF files at the root of this repository (one per documentation
topic, e.g. "Overview of YARP _ Microsoft Learn.pdf") are plain-text
extractions of the original Microsoft Learn pages, kept as a grounding and
fact-checking reference for authoring and reviewing the content above -
see yarp-docs/scripts/content/extract-pdf.mjs. They are not modified or
redistributed beyond their role as an internal authoring aid, and are
covered by the same CC BY 4.0 license and attribution above.

YARP itself
-----------

YARP (Yet Another Reverse Proxy) is an open-source project from the .NET
Foundation, unrelated in license terms to the documentation notice above.
See https://github.com/dotnet/yarp for YARP's own source and license.
